<div class="doc">
  <.link navigate={~p"/steer/docs"} class="back">Back to docs</.link>
  <h1>fm-steer CLI</h1>
  <p class="muted">The captain CLI. It talks only to the firstmate-port HTTP API, never NATS. Ranking, quota math, and provider keys stay server-side.</p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <pre>go build -o fm-steer ./cmd/fm-steer</pre>

  <h2>Auth</h2>
  <p>Device code login stores a JWT at <code>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fm-steer/credentials.json</code> (mode 0600).</p>
  <pre>fm-steer auth login --instance http://localhost:4000
fm-steer auth status
fm-steer auth logout</pre>
  <p><code>FIRSTMATE_INSTANCE</code> sets the default instance.</p>

  <h2>Inbox</h2>
  <pre>fm-steer inbox put --task fm-port --body "hello"
fm-steer inbox next --task fm-port
fm-steer inbox ack --ack &lt;token&gt;
fm-steer inbox list</pre>

  <h2>Route</h2>
  <p>Ask the portal router which worker to use. The answer carries harness, model, effort, and why.</p>
  <pre>fm-steer route "fix the failing test in the ingest controller"
fm-steer route --intel "compare current embedding models"
echo "deploy the portal to production" | fm-steer route</pre>
  <p><code>--intel</code> folds in live OpenRouter and Artificial Analysis inputs. <code>--json</code> prints the full response for scripts and rater agents.</p>

  <h2>Usage</h2>
  <p>Per-account token usage and remaining allowance from the portal ledger.</p>
  <pre>fm-steer usage
fm-steer usage --json</pre>
  <p><code>--json</code> prints the portal's ledger response unchanged, for scripts that need every field.</p>

  <h2>Tenancy</h2>
  <p>Credentials carry the tenant from login. Every request is scoped to that tenant by the API.</p>
</div>
